@startuml 05-sequence-refund-failed-payment
title PayLink - Sequence: Refund a Failed Payment (Phase 1)
skinparam shadowing false
autonumber

actor Customer
participant "Biller Integration /\nRetry job /\nReconciliation" as Source
participant "Payment\nProcessing" as Pay
participant "State machine\n(payment domain)" as SM
participant "Accounts and\nWallet" as Wallet
participant "Notifications" as Notif
participant "Audit" as Audit

== A. The payment becomes Failed ==
alt biller refuses (payment is SentToBiller)
  Source -> Pay : handleBillerResult(paymentId, REFUSED + reason)
  Pay -> SM : SentToBiller -> Failed
else Unknown payment resolved as non-payment
  Source -> Pay : handleBillerResult(paymentId, REFUSED)\nor reconciliation proves non-receipt
  note right
    Only a COMPLETE settlement file can establish
    non-receipt (A-24). Exhausted retries alone
    do NOT trigger a refund (A-06).
  end note
  Pay -> SM : Unknown -> Failed
end
SM --> Pay : transition accepted
Pay -> Pay : save PaymentEvent (from, to, event, details)
Pay -> Audit : record transition (who, when, why)
Pay -> Notif : notify(userId, paymentId, PAYMENT_FAILED, SMS + PUSH)
Notif --> Customer : failure notification with clear reason

== B. Release the hold ==
Pay -> SM : validate Failed -> Refunded
SM --> Pay : allowed
Pay -> Wallet : releaseHold(paymentId)
note right of Wallet
  One transaction with wallet lock (A-07):
  WalletHold ACTIVE -> RELEASED, and RELEASE ledger
  entries move the total from HELD back to AVAILABLE.
  No fee income and no agent commission are posted
  for a failed payment (A-23, US-17).
end note
Wallet --> Pay : hold released, available balance restored
Pay -> SM : Failed -> Refunded
Pay -> Pay : save PaymentEvent (Failed -> Refunded)
Pay -> Audit : record release (who, when, why)
Pay --> Customer : status Refunded (visible in wallet history)

== C. Guard rails ==
opt release requested again (duplicate event or retry)
  Pay -> SM : any transition from Refunded
  SM --> Pay : rejected, Refunded is final
  note right
    The hold is already RELEASED, so no second
    release and no second ledger entry.
  end note
end

opt notification provider is down
  Notif -> Notif : retry up to 3 times, then mark UNDELIVERED
  note right
    The refund still stands; the notification
    failure is tracked separately (US-23).
  end note
end

note over Pay, Wallet
  Out of scope here: refund of a COMPLETED payment (US-27).
  That uses a separate refund request and compensating
  ledger entries; the payment stays Completed (A-12).
end note
@enduml